# A chapter of a seasonal cookbook, on A5 pages printed on both sides: Mirror margins gives the even pages the wide
# margin on the right, and the folios go on the outer edge with two Page overlay, one for the odd pages, with the
# title of the book, and one for the even ones, with the recipe in effect as a running head ({heading 2}). The
# chapter starts at page 87 (Page numbering: restart, First number). The opener has a drop cap (Drop cap: 3), an
# illustration as a numbered Figure ("Plate 1.") and the list of recipes as a Table of contents of the Heading 2
# level. Each recipe starts on a new page with its details on a shared baseline, the ingredients in a List whose
# markers are a leaf drawn in SVG (Marker: image) and the method as a numbered List beside them, in a Grid. The cook's
# notes run around a small illustration (Side: right), the variations and the method of the cake go in two Columns,
# and the quantities of the cake are a Table with a numbered caption and a cell that spans two columns. The body
# text is IBM Plex Serif, justified with optimal line breaking and hyphenation (Language: en-GB).
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
